// @test: run-interpreter
// @tier: 0
// @level: L1
// @tags: modules, mount, variant-constructor, namespace-precedence, regression
// @timeout: 5000
// @expected-exit: 0

/// T0704 pin — an EXPLICITLY MOUNTED zero-arg FUNCTION must silence a
/// same-named ambient variant constructor.
///
/// The collision this pins (measured in the shipped stdlib):
///   * `core/money/currency.vr` declares
///     `public fn inr() -> Currency` (a zero-arg factory), while
///   * `core/math/hott.vr` declares `inr(b: B)` as a variant
///     constructor of the HoTT `Pushout` sum type.
///
/// `variant_constructor_parents` is an AMBIENT flat bare-name table —
/// a prelude.  Before the fix, the T0525 namespace-precedence rule
/// consulted only the TYPE surface of the mounted module, so the
/// mounted FUNCTION lost the bare name to the stranger constructor
/// and the call failed with `inr expects 1 argument(s), got 0`.
///
/// Rule (2) MOUNTED-ITEM PRECEDENCE now consults the VALUE namespace
/// too (`module_publishes_fn`, the `module_publishes_type` twin):
/// when `inr` is explicitly mounted and the mounted module publishes
/// it as a function, the ambient constructor table must DECLINE.
mount core.money.currency.{Currency, inr, usd};

fn main() {
    let c = inr();
    assert_eq(c.code, "INR");
    let u = usd();
    assert_eq(u.code, "USD");
    print(c.code);
}
